Apply the shared-library name infix only to the shared model.

On darwin*, configure sets cf_cv_shlib_version_infix=yes because macOS
uses ABI-versioned dylib names. The library-naming block below keys off
that flag WITHOUT checking whether the model being named is actually
shared, so it rewrites cf_libname and cf_dir_suffix for the NORMAL (.a)
and DEBUG (_g.a) models too.

With --enable-widec --with-termlib=tinfo that produces a Makefile that
contradicts itself -- Libs_To_Make renames ncursesw to tinfo while
mk-1st.awk is invoked with tinfo+w -- and make dies with "No rule to
make target ../lib/libtinfo.a". Linux escapes it because the flag
defaults to no there.

Host-only: this is about naming host dylibs, and the cross-compiled
ncurses never builds a shared model.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -31216,7 +31216,7 @@
 
  			cf_dir_suffix=
  			old_cf_suffix="$cf_suffix"
- 			if test "$cf_cv_shlib_version_infix" = yes ; then
+ 			if test "$cf_cv_shlib_version_infix" = yes && test "$cf_item" = shared ; then
 			if test -n "$USE_LIB_SUFFIX" ; then
 				case "$USE_LIB_SUFFIX" in
 				(tw*)
